
Prepare the KB Admin application for full production deployment on Microsoft Azure, including database migration.

IMPORTANT REQUIREMENTS

- Do NOT change the existing application architecture.
- Do NOT break any existing functionality.
- Preserve all APIs, routes, authentication, permissions, MCP tools, LangSmith integration, Knowledge Base features, Ticketing module, Markdown editor, Workflow engine and existing UI.
- Only make the application production-ready for Azure.

========================================
PHASE 1 - PROJECT ANALYSIS
========================================

Analyze the complete project and identify:

- Framework (Next.js)
- Database technology currently used
- ORM (Prisma/Drizzle/TypeORM/etc.)
- Current database connection
- Environment variables
- Authentication
- Storage requirements
- Static assets
- Existing GitHub Actions
- Build process
- Startup process

Generate a deployment report before making changes.

========================================
PHASE 2 - AZURE DATABASE MIGRATION
========================================

Migrate the existing database to Azure.

If PostgreSQL:
→ Azure Database for PostgreSQL Flexible Server

If MySQL:
→ Azure Database for MySQL Flexible Server

If SQL Server:
→ Azure SQL Database

Requirements:

- Generate migration scripts
- Preserve existing schema
- Preserve relationships
- Preserve indexes
- Preserve constraints
- Preserve foreign keys
- Preserve triggers if any
- Preserve seed data
- Preserve production compatibility

Create:

database/
    migrate.sql
    seed.sql
    backup.sql
    rollback.sql

Update environment variables to support Azure database connection.

========================================
PHASE 3 - DATA MIGRATION
========================================

Create safe migration utilities.

Requirements:

- Export current data
- Import into Azure
- Validate row counts
- Validate foreign keys
- Verify integrity
- Log migration progress
- Rollback support
- Retry failed operations

Generate migration documentation.

========================================
PHASE 4 - APPLICATION CONFIGURATION
========================================

Update the application for Azure.

Configure:

- Production environment
- Database connection pooling
- Secure secrets
- Health endpoint
- Logging
- Error handling
- Production caching
- Compression
- Static assets

========================================
PHASE 5 - AZURE APP SERVICE
========================================

Prepare deployment for Azure App Service.

Configure:

- Production build
- Startup command
- Health checks
- Environment variables
- Application Insights integration
- HTTPS
- Logging
- Scaling compatibility

Do NOT deploy automatically.

========================================
PHASE 6 - GITHUB ACTIONS
========================================

Update the existing GitHub Actions pipeline.

Pipeline should:

Build application

Run tests

Run lint

Run database migrations

Deploy to Azure App Service

Verify deployment

Health check

Rollback on failure

Do NOT create duplicate workflows.

========================================
PHASE 7 - AZURE RESOURCES
========================================

Generate deployment documentation for:

Azure Resource Group

Azure App Service

Azure Database

Azure Storage Account (if needed)

Application Insights

Azure Key Vault (recommended)

Networking requirements

Firewall rules

Connection strings

========================================
PHASE 8 - SECURITY
========================================

Move all secrets to Azure App Settings / Azure Key Vault.

Never commit secrets.

Support:

DATABASE_URL

NEXTAUTH_SECRET

JWT_SECRET

LangSmith keys

API keys

Storage keys

========================================
